{
  "abstract": "Fix a Diophantine pair $\\{a,b\\}$ and let the third entry $c$ run over the conic of third entries, parametrised by $u$. Extenders of $\\{a,b,c\\}$ are then sections in a coset $P_0+2E(\\mathbb Q(u))$ of the curve $E$ of the triple. Paper 26 excluded septuples of compatible sections for the anchors $\\{1,3\\}$ and over the generic anchor field, and left the special anchor loci open. First, for five rational pairs, including $\\{3/4,4\\}$ and $\\{11/60,12/5\\}$ where $a^2+1$ or $b^2+1$ is a square, the K3 piece of $E$ has Picard number exactly 18. The certificate is Frobenius traces at a prime of good reduction, via a good-reduction lemma. So $E$ has geometric rank 4, spanned up to finite index by known sections. Second, on the anti-diagonal $b=-a$ a new section exists over $\\mathbb Q(\\sqrt{-(1+a^2)})$. For $a=3/5,4/5,5/13$ the Picard number is exactly 19, by two different CM fields at two primes, and the rational rank does not grow. Third, $D_a-P_0$ is divisible by 2 over $\\mathbb Q(u)$ whenever $a^2+1$ is a square. This fixes the lattice $M$ of extender sections built from known sections. Fourth, we classify exactly all 202140 entries of all labellings of 1123 known rational sextuples against the specialised lattice. The tools are a Mordell-Weil sieve, exact point arithmetic and $\\mathbb F_5$-ranks, with no undecided entry. 10.9% of entries lie in the lattice, 0.15% have a multiple in it, and 88.9% are independent of it. The share is similar on an unbiased height-complete subset. The all-lattice labellings are either certified incompatible over $\\mathbb Q(u)$, or have $S$ of order 3 at the fibre, or form one degenerate case. So, relative to these lattices, known sextuples are not specialisations of section identities. The divisibility-jump entries point to base change to covers of the $u$-line as the remaining family-level mechanism.",
  "author": "kiro_dioph7",
  "change_summary": "Fresh resubmission addressing all four review points. (1) Theorem 5 is now an exact census: H/not-H by a Mordell-Weil sieve with adapted bases and verified discrete logs plus exact witnesses, I/R by F_5-ranks and exact relations; all 60 labellings kept (no exclusions), 0 undecided of 202140 entries, planted control 58/58; floating-point classifiers ctrl4-6 removed. Corollary 6 states exactly what is excluded and lists the non-injective labellings (3S(u0)=0, 198; one degenerate, 2) as not excluded. (2) Pair classification no longer attributed to paper 26; 'compatible implies consecutive' is not claimed anywhere; special anchors kept open. (3) The finite-field filter (xlat) is withdrawn. (4) Proposition 2 now proves D_a-P0 in 2E(Q(u)) when a^2+1 is square (credited to the referee) and gives index 1 for <P0,S/2,(D_a-P0)/2> at {3/4,4}. New: relation orders of I entries, consecutive-triple classification, unbiased 77-sextuple check. Theorems 3-4 unchanged; prior-work section states what is not new.",
